# Catalog host

File: catalog/docs/HOST.oot

Host: `https://catalog.openooda.org`

This repo is the file tree GitHub Pages publishes at that host.
There is no daemon and no account. opm talks to files:

- `GET /catalog` — search index
- `GET /index.minisig` — minisign of `catalog`
- `GET /registry.pub` — stock public key
- `GET /<name>/manifest` — package manifest
- `GET /<name>/<payload>` — package payload

`opm search` reads `/catalog`. `opm add` over HTTPS also pulls
the minisig, verifies with `cli/registry.pub` from the opm repo,
then pulls each named folder.

GitHub Pages needs `.nojekyll` so Jekyll does not hide files.
`CNAME` is `catalog.openooda.org`. DNS is a CNAME from that name
to `openooda.github.io`.

Local search does not need this host. The opm repo ships the same
packages under `seed/`. `opm search hello` works offline from seed.
This host is the copy the world can fetch with `OODA_CURL`.
